-- statement:
--   Part 1 of 4 of a library proving Artin's approximation theorem at a rational point (M. Artin 1969, Theorem 1.10, étale-neighbourhood form): for a perfect field $K$, a finite-type $K$-algebra $A$ and a $K$-point $\chi : A \to K$, a solution in the $(\ker\chi)$-adic completion $\hat{A}$ of a finite polynomial system over $A$ gives a solution with the same residues in an étale neighbourhood of $\chi$. Everything is stated in Mathlib terms (`MvPolynomial`, `MvPowerSeries`, `AdicCompletion`, `Algebra.Etale`, `Algebra.TensorProduct`). Contents, in dependency order:
--
--   * the Jacobian criterion at the generic point of a prime of a polynomial ring over a perfect field, and the Jacobian datum (a nonvanishing minor) of such a prime;
--   * the coordinate change $x_{i+1} \mapsto x_{i+1} + x_0^{c^{i+1}}$ of $K[[x_0, \dots, x_n]]$, colex-minimal exponents and base-$c$ weights;
